# Line endings are LF in the index and in every working tree.
#
# Previously nothing declared this, so a Windows checkout got CRLF via
# `core.autocrlf` while the index stayed LF. Prettier absorbed the difference
# with `endOfLine: auto`; oxfmt, which replaced it, always writes LF, so
# `pnpm format:check` reported every file as unformatted after each checkout
# on Windows. Declaring the policy here fixes it for every clone regardless of
# the developer's local git configuration, which `core.autocrlf` cannot do.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.sh text eol=lf
